# SABOTAGE: D3 (ADR-046 §4.2) — the pii_declared erasability GUARD at the define
# chokepoint is bypassed: `guard_pii_declared_erasable/3`'s fail-closed final branch
# returns `:ok` instead of `{:error, {:pii_declared_unerasable, table}}`. A tenant can
# then turn on `pii_declared: true` for a table with NO registered custom-bag erasure
# arm — so a live pii_declared bag ships UNERASABLE (its plaintext survives every shred),
# the exact structural hole the guard closes. Flips the guard's REFUSED red-path (a
# spec-less pii_declared define must be rejected) while the WITH-spec positive control
# still passes, so this targets ONLY the guard's fail-closed branch.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/custom_fields_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: REFUSED: a pii_declared field on a table with NO custom-bag erasure spec is rejected
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/custom_fields.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/custom_fields.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/custom_fields.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/custom_fields.ex
@@ -580,7 +580,7 @@
     cond do
       String.starts_with?(table, @object_table_prefix) -> :ok
       erasure_spec_covers?(table, opts) -> :ok
-      true -> {:error, {:pii_declared_unerasable, table}}
+      true -> :ok
     end
   end
 
